# NOTE (ISS-0175 / GH #503): this list is inherited from upstream LuaJIT, where
# `luajit_relver.txt` is correctly ignored because upstream's src/Makefile
# generates it from the LuaJIT repo's own git metadata
# (`git show -s --format=%ct`, Makefile:493-495).
#
# This repo vendors LuaJIT as a snapshot and drives the build from
# vendor/luajit/build.zig instead of that Makefile. There is no LuaJIT `.git`
# here to read, and build.zig consumes the file as a REQUIRED input
# (genversion.addFileArg, build.zig:79) without generating it. Ignoring it made
# every fresh clone and every CI run fail with
# "failed to check cache: ... luajit_relver.txt file_hash FileNotFound".
#
# So `luajit_relver.txt` is deliberately TRACKED here. This mirrors upstream's
# own fallback for non-git consumers (source tarballs), which read a tracked
# `../.relver`. A vendored dependency is the tarball case, not the git case.
#
# The entries below stay ignored and are correct to ignore: unlike
# luajit_relver.txt, build.zig DOES generate every one of them into the Zig
# cache (genversion -> luajit.h; buildvm -> the lj_*def.h set and lj_vm).
luajit
luajit.h
lj_bcdef.h
lj_ffdef.h
lj_libdef.h
lj_recdef.h
lj_folddef.h
lj_vm.[sS]
